{"kind":"symbol","title":"EliasFanoGraph.Edges","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Edges"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The edges of a graph, or a contiguous run of them. Positions are edge indices. Iterating"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"decodes each row once, O(1) amortized per edge; subscripting one position is O(log n +"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out-degree), so prefer iteration to index loops."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Edges"}],"url":"\/documentation\/eliasfanographmodule\/eliasfanograph\/edges-swift.struct","identifier":"doc:\/\/EliasFanoGraphModule\/documentation\/EliasFanoGraphModule\/EliasFanoGraph\/Edges-swift.struct"}}}